title start
kind: note
tags: business-plan audience problem-discovery-method
Audience problem discovery method
title end

paragraph start
Problems are found in the words people already use, not in guesses. Sources: comments under larger accounts, questions in communities, search suggestions and replies to polls on the brand own accounts.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Copy the exact sentence a person wrote, note where it was found and count how often similar sentences appear. A problem seen once is a note. A problem seen often is a finding.
paragraph end

code start
language: text
1 collect exact sentences with their source
2 group sentences that describe the same problem
3 count each group
4 write one plain sentence per group
5 add the groups to the ranked problem list
code end

